@startuml engine_consolidation
' purpose: approved single StarChess physics kernel with distinct admission facades and optional causal effects
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/engine/**
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/index.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/commands/queue-action.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/submit-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/resolve-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/board/vision.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/board/ray-scan.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/model/square.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/engine-consolidation.test.ts
' covers: packages/game-core/src/**
' covers: packages/game-core/tests/compatibility-exports.test.ts
' covers: packages/contracts/tests/shared-engine.e2e.test.ts
' covers: packages/contracts/src/game-session.ts
' covers: packages/policy/src/**
' covers: packages/policy/tests/source-boundary.test.ts
' status: APPROVED GOAL; implementation, final path alignment and fresh verification pending
' related: _spec/ml-runtime-architecture.puml, _spec/game-core.puml, _spec/causal-journal.puml
' related: _spec/turn-planning.puml, _spec/classical-resolution.puml, _spec/turn-resolution.puml
' preserved: SCFEN, SAN, packed replay, AI/helpers and app-facing resolution events remain product contracts
' preserved: afterPending, afterB, bMoves, fMoves and EndScTurnResult retain their timeline meanings
' preserved: causal-state.v1 and causal-journal.v1 retain identity, grouping and target-consumption semantics
' fixes: live own-Marine promotion guard; delayed-swap mine removal synchronized into phase3
' verification: historical counts are not fresh regression results; no native execution or training grant
' template: local template absent; human must fetch and commit once when separately permitted
title PLANNED · One physics kernel, explicit admission facades
left to right direction

component "apps/starchess" as UI <<app>>
component "packages/contracts/src/game-session.ts\nGameSession" as SESSION <<app>>
component "packages/policy/src\nrecipient-local candidates + 2271 features" as POLICY <<app>>
component "packages/game-core/src\ncompatibility forwards only" as COMPAT <<app>>

package "packages/starchess-core" {
  component "src/index.ts\nSCFEN / SAN / replay / AI / helpers" as ROOT <<app>>
  component "src/commands/queue-action.ts\nproduct incoming-action admission" as PRODUCT <<app>>
  component "src/engine/index.ts\nqueue-validation.ts / resolve.ts\nnative ML admission facade" as NATIVE <<app>>
  component "src/resolve/submit-turn.ts\nsrc/resolve/resolve-turn.ts\nshared B / C / F mutation kernel" as KERNEL <<app>>
  component "src/board/vision.ts / ray-scan.ts\nsrc/model/square.ts\nshared geometry + types" as GEOMETRY <<app>>
  component "src/engine/causal-types.ts\nconstructor-free ResolutionEffects" as EFFECTS <<app>>
  component "src/engine/causal-producer.ts\nhost-only begin / end wrappers" as PRODUCER <<app>>
  component "src/engine/causal-events.ts\nprivate per-game CausalJournal" as JOURNAL <<app>>
}

UI --> ROOT : existing product API
ROOT --> PRODUCT : soft incoming actions
ROOT --> KERNEL : product begin / end / resolve
SESSION --> NATIVE : native queue admission
SESSION --> PRODUCER : journaled begin / end
NATIVE --> KERNEL : dependency-checked actions
PRODUCER --> NATIVE : same native validation contract
PRODUCER --> JOURNAL : create per-call collector
JOURNAL ..> EFFECTS : implements sink contract
KERNEL ..> EFFECTS : optional per-game sink
KERNEL --> GEOMETRY : shared physical rules
COMPAT ..> NATIVE : reexports, no algorithms
COMPAT ..> PRODUCER : host-only compatibility subpath
POLICY ..> NATIVE : pure rules / planning only
SESSION --> POLICY : recipient observations via runtime

note bottom of PRODUCT
  Product queues accept soft incoming actions
  without applying the ML contract for classical
  dependencies. That difference controls
  admission only, so both paths still use the
  same board geometry and physical rules.
end note

note top of NATIVE
  Native validation checks classical dependencies
  before the shared kernel resolves an accepted
  queue. Journaling cannot select this contract,
  because adding a sink must not change which
  actions the engine accepts.
end note

note bottom of EFFECTS
  Each mutation group captures live vision before
  units die or ordered mines leave the board.
  This common preimage preserves causal witnesses
  that final snapshots cannot justify after their
  vision source disappears.
end note

note right of JOURNAL
  Deferred discovery records only the target
  consumed by a successful live operation.
  Mine order and stable IDs survive board
  reparsing, while each requested deploy
  distinguishes no birth from immediate death.
end note

note top of KERNEL
  A promotion requires a surviving Marine of the
  action's own color at the destination.
  A stale queued promotion must not transform an
  enemy replacement or another unit.
end note

note bottom of KERNEL
  Delayed swaps synchronize mine removals into
  the phase-three snapshot after each actual
  contact. Otherwise a detonated mine survives in
  the final snapshot despite its recorded
  destruction.
end note

note bottom of COMPAT
  Compatibility paths forward exports without
  retaining their own algorithms or resolver
  branches. Export identity and source checks
  must prevent any future return of a second
  physics kernel.
end note

note top of SESSION
  The session owns banks and paid receipts
  outside the physics kernel rather than
  inferring costs from survivors. Policy sees
  recipient-local observations, and its source
  closure must exclude the private host producer.
end note

note bottom of GEOMETRY
  Local Square union.
  Product vision keeps { fen() }.
end note

note bottom of POLICY
  Earlier fixture counts describe historical
  source rather than fresh proof of this engine
  change. New JavaScript and TypeScript checks
  remain pending, with no native execution or
  approval for game-data training.
end note
@enduml
